🧠 Logic Used In This Project

This project uses a rule-based password evaluation algorithm.

Instead of machine learning, the logic focuses on industry-standard password requirements.

Step 1 → Password Length Validation
if len(password) >= 8:
    score += 1
Why?

Long passwords increase:

Entropy
Search space
Brute-force resistance

Short passwords are easier to crack.

Step 2 → Uppercase Detection
re.search(r"[A-Z]", password)
Why?

Uppercase characters:

Increase combinations
Improve complexity
Reduce predictability

Example:

password ❌
Password ✅
Step 3 → Lowercase Detection
re.search(r"[a-z]", password)
Why?

Mixing character sets improves randomness.

Step 4 → Number Detection
re.search(r"\d", password)
Why?

Numbers expand attack complexity.

Example:

hello
↓

hello123
Step 5 → Special Character Detection
re.search(r"[!@#$%^&*(),.?\":{}|<>]")
Why?

Special symbols greatly increase possible combinations.

Example:

Password123

↓

P@ssw0rd#123
Step 6 → Score Calculation

Each successful rule:

+1 Point

Total:

5 Points Maximum

Classification:

0–2 → Weak

3–4 → Medium

5 → Strong
Step 7 → Secure Password Generation

Generator logic:

random.choice()

Used to:

Select random characters
Build unpredictable passwords
Avoid repetitive patterns

Generated password loops until:

Score ≥ 3

This ensures generated passwords meet minimum strength requirements.

